## Final Judgement
**Summary of Key Insights:**
The fact-check reveals that a viral WhatsApp hoax in India around October 2020 used the file name "India is doing it" and falsely claimed to contain a video showing India's COVID-19 curve flattening, but multiple sources confirm it was a hoax without any evidence of an actual malicious file. Meanwhile, epidemiological data indicates India's COVID-19 curve was rising sharply in mid-October 2020, not flattening, and no reputable outlets reported a real malware campaign using COVID-19 curve data as bait at that time.

**Missing Information:**
No further information is lacking; the available evidence clearly addresses the claim's key elements.

**Conclusion:**
The claim is explicitly refuted by the evidence, as it asserts the presence of a malicious file in a message about India's flattening COVID-19 curve, but fact-checks identified the message as a hoax with no malicious file, and the curve was not flattening at the time. Therefore, the decision is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The claim is refuted because fact-checks by [BOOM](https://www.boomlive.in/fast-check/hoax-message-claims-india-is-doing-it-video-will-hack-your-phone-10210) and [The Quint](https://www.thequint.com/news/webqoof/india-is-doing-it-video-will-hack-your-phone-hoax-message) identified the viral WhatsApp message about a file named "India is doing it" as a hoax, with no evidence of an actual malicious file. Furthermore, epidemiological data from [CNN](https://www.cnn.com/2020/08/31/asia/india-reopening-coronavirus-surge-intl-hnk/index.html) indicates India's COVID-19 curve was rising sharply in mid-October 2020, not flattening, and no reputable outlets reported a real malware campaign using this lure.